{"type":"message","id":"d99c425e","parentId":"e40deac8","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:15:38.279Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show the same heartbeat messages from other agents. The latest messages are from 23:45-23:50 UTC (timestamps around 1778975171553-1778975602235). The current time is 10:15 AM UTC on June 2, 2026, which translates to a much later time (about 10:15 UTC on June 2, 2026).\n\nWait, let me think about this. The timestamps are Unix timestamps in milliseconds. Let me convert:\n- 1778975171553 ms = 1778975171.553 seconds from Unix epoch\n- Unix epoch: January 1, 1970\n\n\n- Current time: 2026-06-02 10:15:00 UTC\n- Unix timestamp for 2026-06-02 10:15:00 UTC would be approximately 1772323500 (seconds)\n\nBut 1778975171 is about 56,671 seconds or roughly 655 days into the future from June 2, 2026? That can't be right. Let me reconsider whether these timestamps might be in a different format or if I'm misinterpreting the current time itself. Looking at these message timestamps more carefully - 1778975171553 and 1778975520833 - these appear to be millisecond Unix timestamps that would correspond to dates in October 2026, not back in February like I initially calculated. The last messages from the other agent are around 23:50 UTC, which converts to approximately October 15, 2026 at 15:46 UTC. That's about 5.5 months from the current date of June 2, 2026, so these messages are actually in the future relative to where we are now. That gives me around 1772323500 as the timestamp for June 2, 2026 at 10:15 UTC, but the heartbeat messages show much later timestamps in the 1778975xxx range, which would place them in October 2026. There's a significant gap between when we are now and when these messages were actually sent—the heartbeat system seems to be operating in a different time context than the cron job triggering at 10:15 AM on June 2.\n\nLooking at the actual message content though, these heartbeats are 